# AGENTS.md

**All working knowledge for this repo lives in [`knowledge/`](knowledge/INDEX.md) — read [knowledge/INDEX.md](knowledge/INDEX.md) FIRST and check its KB status line.**

- If the status is **SCAFFOLDED**: the knowledge base is structure-only. Complete `knowledge/_bootstrap-brief.md` (distillation pass) before citing anything in `knowledge/` as truth.
- If the status is **VERIFIED @ &lt;commit&gt;**: cite freely; recheck runtime claims against the environment before operational work.

## Search, don't read

Route by question type BEFORE reaching for Grep/Read:

| Question about | Tool |
|---|---|
| Knowledge/rules/architecture (`knowledge/` content) | `python3 scripts/ksearch.py "<query>"` — ranked excerpts + file pointers; read the TL;DR before the full file |
| Code: where to start, callers, blast radius, uses | `ripwire <source-dir> --for="<task>"` / `--callers=<SYM>` / `--impact=<SYM>` / `--uses=<SYM>` if installed; else targeted `rg` + read |
| String literals, configs, non-code files | `rg` |

Before adding a helper or completing work, follow the [tool and verification commands](knowledge/practices/commands.md). Ripwire is static evidence; run the project's actual checks.

## Work across sessions

Check the [plans board](knowledge/plans/README.md) for ownership before changing files. To save or resume work, follow [kb-handoff](knowledge/practices/skills/kb-handoff.md). Other [skills](knowledge/practices/skills/README.md) are available as needed; their discovery stubs share these canonical procedures.

## Write-back policy — knowledge goes HERE, never to your native memory

1. **Default is DON'T write.** Record only what a future session would otherwise re-derive painfully or dangerously.
2. New facts, lessons, pitfalls, rules → `knowledge/` (right subdir per INDEX.md), not your home-dir memory/learning files.
3. **Commit knowledge changes with the code that taught them.**
4. Stale code/docs found during work get REMOVED/updated in the same commit.
5. **Don't duplicate**: `ksearch` first; patch the existing file.

Full policy: [knowledge/rules/write-back-policy.md](knowledge/rules/write-back-policy.md).
